//? Title: I3D:random temporal inflation and visible tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original KTH clips feed all57inflated3Dunits and nine Mixed modules. Visible tensor Adam,population BN state,complete data previews and every held-out error expose what the short RGB-only fit actually learns.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/i3d.cpp`.

> The method

Inflate random spatial filters equally over time,preserve the complete RGB I3D graph and source offset-only population BN,then show every optimizer and moving-state update. Select paired checkpoints on validation and restore RGB-only inference before complete held-out and temporal-control comparisons.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/i3d_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/i3d_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/i3d_concept.tikz > build/i3d_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/i3d_concept.svg build/i3d_concept.dvi > build/i3d_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
