> Sonnet-v1 population moments,without a gamma scale

Each normalized unit learns W and beta only,no convolution bias or gamma.
Use eps.001 and moving decay.999,initial mean0/variance1. Training uses batch
population moments;moving variance is also population variance,without the
unbiased correction used by the previous factorized networks' fused BN.
Train-without-update leaves moving arrays unchanged. Inference freezes them.

A hand-checkable four-value fixture exposes the difference:W1,beta0,input1..4,
mean2.5,population variance1.25. With decay.5,the new moving mean is1.25 and
variance1.125. These are a declared fixture,not fitting-population calibration.
The actual report fit preserves source decay.999 and performs no extra calibration.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/i3d_population.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore p(1), state(2);
  const auto x = n::arange(1, 5).reshape({2, 1, 1, 2, 1});
  m::I3dUnit(p, state, "u", x, 1, 1, 1, false, .5, false);
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    p.set("u/W", n::ones({1, 1, 1, 1, 1}));
  }
  const auto before = state.flatten();
  const auto unchanged = m::I3dUnit(p, state, "u", x, 1, 1, 1, true, .5, false);
  if (before != state.flatten())
    return 1;
  const auto trained = m::I3dUnit(p, state, "u", x, 1, 1, 1, true, .5, true);
  const auto inference = m::I3dUnit(p, state, "u", x, 1, 1, 1, false, .5, false);
  const auto expected = n::relu((x - 2.5) / std::sqrt(1.25 + .001));
  const auto parity = n::max(n::abs(trained - expected));
  if (parity.item() > 2e-7 || std::abs(state.at("u/mean").item() - 1.25) > 1e-7 ||
      std::abs(state.at("u/variance").item() - 1.125) > 1e-7)
    return 1;
  std::print("Population BN mean {},variance {},every output parity {:.9g};gamma "
             "absent,{}learned/{}moving leaves.\n",
             state.at("u/mean"), state.at("u/variance"), parity.item(), p.size(),
             state.size());
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(n::arange(1, 5).to_vector<double>(), trained.reshape({4}).to_vector<double>(),
             "batch moments", {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(n::arange(1, 5).to_vector<double>(), inference.reshape({4}).to_vector<double>(),
             "moving moments", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Declared population-moment BN fixture")
      .x_label("original scalar input1..4")
      .y_label("actual normalized/ReLU output");
  plot.save_svg("build/i3d_population.svg");
}
```
