> Verification and limits

Six native tests check all196inflation/source-input and14population-unit host
finite differences,the actual full64x224graph/every116learned derivative,
every57initialized filter's temporal slices,all moving-state mutation modes,
an independent four-value population-variance oracle and invalid contracts.
Shared video tests check every1769472original resized pixel and every reference
feature/score. Every public example and the original three-epoch workflow pass.
The learned model remains near a balanced tie and below motion1NN accuracy;
it predicts boxing for all six clips,with recalls1/0/0 and NLL1.098270.
Epoch3 is selected with validation NLL1.098550. The fixed fitting inference
NLL slightly worsens1.098623920->1.098829636. No hidden calibration or
published pretrained benchmark result is substituted for this outcome.

> Conclusion

Full graph and independent derivative checks pass,but the short random-initialized fit stays near chance and does not improve fixed fitting inference NLL. Complete source data and moving-state semantics support an implementation example without a pretrained Kinetics accuracy claim.

> References

- [Carreira and Zisserman(2017),Quo Vadis,Action Recognition? A New Model and the Kinetics Dataset](https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.07750).
- [Original KTH action data](https://www.csc.kth.se/cvap/actions/).
